Z||000000||Greg Piet||02-18-2000||01:47 AM||||Where did you MSD owners install your ignition box?  Im looking for a good spot, and I'm not sure where would be best.  I was afraid that if I mounted it by the blower on the passenger side, the blower might cause interference.  And if I mount it on the drivers side of the trunk I have to extend the power cables.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||02-18-2000||02:08 AM||||I have mine mounted on the passenger side in the trunk (88 formula, no blower).  I doubt that the blower would interfere with the MSD box. It may even offer some additional cooling if you could port some kind of opening so that air would blow on it.  <P>Note :  <BR>     Even on a hot day with considerable driving time my MSD box will be only moderatly hot to the touch, so the air venting idea may not be important enough to even consider.<P>Mike||||reg||1
